---
import ComponentDoc from '../../layouts/ComponentDoc.astro';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';
import Preview from '@esa/docs/Preview.astro';
import Api from '@esa/docs/Api.astro';
import PropsTable from '@esa/docs/PropsTable.astro';
import { withBase } from '@esa/docs/base';

const methods = [
  { name: 'show(config)', type: 'method', description: 'Shows a toast. config: { message, variant?, duration?, action?, dismissable?, uniqueKey? }. Returns its id.' },
  { name: 'success / info / warning / danger(msg, config?)', type: 'method', description: 'Shorthands for show() with that variant.' },
  { name: 'dismiss(id)', type: 'method', description: 'Removes the toast with that id.' },
  { name: 'clearAll()', type: 'method', description: 'Removes every active toast.' },
];

const config = [
  { name: 'message', type: 'string', description: 'Toast body text.' },
  { name: 'variant', type: "'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger'", default: "'info'", description: 'Color and leading icon.' },
  { name: 'duration', type: 'number', default: '0', description: 'Auto-dismiss delay in ms. 0 (the default) keeps the toast until dismissed. This default changed from 5000 on 2026-08-16 — a timer the user cannot adjust is WCAG 2.2.1 Timing Adjustable, a Level A failure. Passing a duration still works and still auto-dismisses; it opts you out of 2.2.1 unless you provide the adjustment yourself.' },
  { name: 'action', type: 'string', description: 'Optional action button label. Discouraged — see Accessibility below. Only safe when the same action is also reachable in the page itself.' },
  { name: 'dismissable', type: 'boolean', default: 'true', description: 'Renders the close button.' },
  { name: 'uniqueKey', type: 'string', description: 'Dedupe key. A second show() with the same key does not stack a second toast, but it DOES re-announce the message and restart any countdown — the second occurrence is a real event.' },
];

const props = [
  { name: 'label', type: 'string', default: "'Notifications'", description: 'Accessible name for the region landmark that wraps the stack. Change it only if a page has more than one stack.' },
];

const events = [
  { name: 'snackbar-action', type: 'CustomEvent<{ id: string }>', description: "Fired when a toast's action button is pressed." },
];
---
<ComponentDoc name="Snackbar Container" category="Overlays" slug="esa-snackbar-container" type="wc" status="stable"
  summary="Bottom-right toast stack. Drive it imperatively — <code>show(config)</code>, the variant shorthands, <code>dismiss(id)</code>, and <code>clearAll()</code>. Defaults to info / persistent / dismissable, with <code>uniqueKey</code> dedupe. Messages are announced through the shared announcer, not by the stack itself.">

  <Section id="preview" title="Preview">
    <p>Place one container on the page, then call its methods: <code>el.success('Saved.')</code>.</p>
    <Preview code={`<button data-kind="success">Success</button>

<esa-snackbar-container id="toasts"></esa-snackbar-container>`}>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="info">Info</button>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="success">Success</button>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="warning">Warning</button>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="danger">Danger</button>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="action">With action</button>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="timed">Auto-dismiss (5s)</button>
      <button class="trigger" data-kind="clear">Clear all</button>
      <esa-snackbar-container id="toasts"></esa-snackbar-container>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="api" title="API">
    <h3>Methods</h3>
    <PropsTable rows={methods} />
    <h3>Config object (show)</h3>
    <PropsTable rows={config} />
    <h3>Attributes</h3>
    <PropsTable rows={props} />
    <Api events={events} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="accessibility" title="Accessibility">
    <p>
      Toasts are the hardest common pattern to make accessible, and most implementations
      fail. This one is built persistent-first: the timed, animated version is the
      enhancement, not the baseline.
    </p>

    <h3>The stack is not a live region</h3>
    <p>
      Announcing is handled by the shared announcer (<code>@esa/ecology/announcer</code>),
      which owns the only two live regions in the kit — one polite, one assertive, in the
      light DOM, mounted before anything happens. Putting <code>aria-live</code> on this
      stack instead would fail three ways: each toast is created and populated in the same
      tick, so the region would be born with its content and never announce; the text sits
      two shadow roots deep, where live-region observation is unreliable; and every page
      with a stack would own a third region competing with the other two.
    </p>
    <p>
      What the stack does carry is <code>role="region"</code> with a name, so it is a
      landmark. An announcement tells someone a toast exists; the landmark is how they
      get to it.
    </p>

    <h3>Timing (SC 2.2.1, Level A)</h3>
    <ul class="a11y">
      <li><code>duration</code> now defaults to <code>0</code> — the toast stays until dismissed. That is the only configuration that conforms without extra work.</li>
      <li>If you pass a duration, hovering or focusing the stack pauses every countdown. That helps pointer and keyboard users. It does <strong>not</strong> help someone reading with a screen reader's virtual cursor, which fires neither event — so pausing is a mitigation, not a conformance argument.</li>
      <li><kbd>Esc</kbd> dismisses the newest toast, but only while focus is inside the stack. A global handler would let someone closing a tooltip destroy a toast they had not read.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Action buttons</h3>
    <p>
      <code>action</code> is supported and discouraged. A live region announces raw text
      with no roles, so "Undo" is read as a bare word with nothing to say it is a button;
      focus is never moved to it; and there is no mechanism to navigate to a toast. Add one
      only when the same action is <em>also</em> available in the page. If the toast is the
      only route to it, that is not a status message — use
      <a href={withBase('/components/esa-dialog')}>esa-dialog</a>, which moves focus and
      persists.
    </p>

    <ul class="a11y">
      <li>Dismissing a toast that held focus returns focus to wherever it came from, rather than dropping it to <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>Below 30rem the stack becomes a full-width strip instead of a 420px box overflowing the viewport (SC 1.4.10 Reflow, 1.4.4 Resize).</li>
      <li>Each toast renders an <a href={withBase('/components/esa-snackbar-item')}>esa-snackbar-item</a> with a 32px dismiss target and a visible focus ring.</li>
      <li>The newest toast appears at the bottom of the stack (column-reverse), nearest the user's attention.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

</ComponentDoc>

<script>
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-snackbar-container';

  const toasts = document.getElementById('toasts') as any;
  document.querySelectorAll('.trigger').forEach((btn) =>
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const kind = (btn as HTMLElement).dataset.kind;
      switch (kind) {
        case 'info': toasts.info('A neutral notification.'); break;
        case 'success': toasts.success('Changes saved.'); break;
        case 'warning': toasts.warning('Low disk space.'); break;
        case 'danger': toasts.danger('Upload failed.'); break;
        case 'action': toasts.show({ message: 'Item archived.', variant: 'success', action: 'Undo' }); break;
        // The opt-in path, shown next to the default so the difference is visible.
        // Hover or focus the stack while this one is counting down — it pauses.
        case 'timed': toasts.show({ message: 'Auto-dismisses in 5s.', duration: 5000 }); break;
        case 'clear': toasts.clearAll(); break;
      }
    }),
  );
</script>

<style>
  .trigger {
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-200, 0.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-strong, #d4d4d4);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-raised, #fff);
    color: var(--color-content-default, #171717);
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: var(--font-size-200, 0.9375rem);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>
